# Build outputs and local state never enter an image's build context.
**/target
**/node_modules
**/.test-out
**/__pycache__
client/dist
bench/results
tests/fuzz/corpus
tests/fuzz/artifacts
tests/fuzz/results
tests/fuzz/coverage
.git
# What no image reads, so a change to it rebuilds nothing: the documentation and the static pages, the installer, the
# Compose files, the public demo's installation, CI, and the scripts (but the three the display's build runs, the one
# that makes the Rust builds' dependency skeleton, and the notices every image carries, which scripts/notices.py writes
# with LICENSE and the texts in scripts/notices/).
docs
site
*.md
install.sh
compose*.yaml
demo
.github
scripts
!scripts/svt-av1.sh
!scripts/opus.sh
!scripts/static-library.sh
!scripts/skeleton.sh
!scripts/notices.py
!scripts/notices
# Host inputs: Compose's variables.
.env
# Images take their toolchain from the pinned rust base image; the file's extra components would need the network.
rust-toolchain.toml
